# =============================================================================
# The app's own settings: the committed declaration of every variable that YOUR code reads and
# that no capability declares. Names only: nothing loads this file.
#
# `.env` is generated by `mistral apps init` / `capability add` from the `envVars` of each
# installed capability, and it is gitignored. A setting you add in `packages/py/env/src/env/<name>.py`
# has no capability to declare it, so give it its default on the settings field and declare its
# name here, with no value:
#
#     # packages/py/env/src/env/my_feature.py:  my_feature_model: str = "mistral-medium-latest"
#     MY_FEATURE_MODEL=
#
# The field default applies wherever the variable is unset, so `.env` needs no matching line; add
# one to `.env` only to override it locally. Do not copy this file over `.env`: it holds no
# capability settings.
#
# `tests/test_composed_env_contract.py` (shipped by the testing capability) checks that every
# settings field is declared either by an installed capability or here, and that every line here
# is empty, so a default never lives in two places.
# =============================================================================
OCR_MODEL=
MATCHING_MODEL=
